# This directory contains scripts for running experiments

## exp2-run.sh: one scripted run for experiment 2, on localhost.

Starts a capture on the loopback interface, the relay, a silent listener and a talker whose input comes from the
traffic generator. When the generator is done, it waits a few seconds for the last cells and stops everything. It only
automates what would otherwise be typed by hand every time.

Usage: scripts/exp2-run.sh <bin-dir> <seed> <out-dir> [generator flags...]
   bin-dir   bin/ for the normal build, bin/nocover/ for the no-cover build
   seed      the generator's -seed
   out-dir   created by the script; must not exist yet. Keep it outside the
             repository: captures are never committed.
   generator flags, e.g. -duration 2m, are passed on to the generator.

Leaves in out-dir:
   capture.pcapng                  everything on port 9735
   talker.timing, listener.timing  the clients' timing logs (-timing)
   phases.log                      the generator's phase log (the labels)
   listener.out                    the lines the listener printed
   *.err                           each program's stderr
   run.info                        arguments, times and the binaries' build info

Needs dumpcap with capture rights for the current user (e.g. membership of the wireshark group), and the port free.